#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111660} :activity/id #uuid "a679a0bc-f291-575b-bac5-97356c792140" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049799 :topic/id #uuid "14d86bef-ffa1-58b3-9249-a9e29d8bde2a" :topic/math-academy-id 1540} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111660 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111894 :tutorial/content "The graph of the square root function $y=\\sqrt{x}$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/a4/a4d6f457f29cc6a292f23029967dc6fbb0c0f3905a04f34a430fddc8b211b0c3.png)\n\n  \n\nIn this lesson, we will learn how to apply graph transformations to the square root function. Let's start by considering translations." :tutorial/id #uuid "ff943ba5-7959-599a-8f13-e5bdb1bda83a" :tutorial/math-academy-id 4775 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "2d1bbdf9-422b-5f69-8f59-21d910778f63" :step/math-academy-id 464534 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111661}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111661 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111895 :tutorial/content "We can move the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}$ up or down by adding or subtracting a number. For example, to obtain the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}-3$ we perform the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n- Translate the graph **down** by $3$ units to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}-3.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](images/1b/1b5eadb281202323377386e6b750a304ece8f39232d0c37dc5d4885004a6b588.png)\n\nSimilarly, we can also move the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}$ to the left or to the right by adding or subtracting a number to the variable $x$ under the square root. For instance,  to obtain the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x-3},$ we perform the following transformations:  \n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n- Translate the graph to the **right** by $3$ units to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x-3}.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](images/6d/6d51b569648468c78445daa6b8dc658fe6e2e8cb24ca8308b60a1f40b07c7e29.png)\n\nRemember:\n\n- Shifting a function up/down/left/right does *not*  change the shape of a graph.\n\n- If $a$ is a positive number, then a transformation of the type $y=f(x\\pm a)$ is *counter-intuitive*: $f(x+a)$ moves the graph to the *left* by $a$ units, while $f(x-a)$ moves the graph to the *right* by $a$ units." :tutorial/id #uuid "7bdd8c52-b035-531e-b5ba-085731e44771" :tutorial/math-academy-id 4776 :tutorial/title "Vertical and Horizontal Translations"} :step/id #uuid "91171f12-b0b8-5ca8-afcf-bde7eb9fb6fe" :step/math-academy-id 464535 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111662}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111662 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110708 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110531 :question/id #uuid "04070131-1543-5516-a7f1-509ea3f01234" :question/math-academy-id "e-7937"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a70b1e82-4650-5de9-ad47-7578481b802a" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048419} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050647} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050753}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111011} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111013} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557241}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Square Root Function Containing One Translation"} :step/id #uuid "66c173b6-94ff-5b36-988c-72a5f4e6623b" :step/math-academy-id 464536 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111663}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111663 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110709 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110532 :question/id #uuid "0e964fdb-fa9e-516a-badf-2217a7937bc8" :question/math-academy-id "e-7938"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3425852-1b32-552e-baaf-bf53644e53b8" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111014} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111164} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557257} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557261} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557299} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557322}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Square Root Function Containing Two Translations"} :step/id #uuid "fd64edda-d116-5987-a423-30af039a0c48" :step/math-academy-id 464539 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111664}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111664 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111896 :tutorial/content "We can reflect the graph of the square root function ![](images/35/35f3311d1bf6feffd9b0cdb6b4910ebf8111065bbec512558385afb246b30e0d.svg) in both the ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg) and ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-axes.\n\nMultiplying ![](images/99/99daf2e095b0105b7aaf495a7c3d901cc574d0dc8dc7e67294fbced0edbaf920.svg) by ![](images/66/66ef4b5796888b4025ee2d8b3d516ec80741b341db9389696b6e77a4af5208d8.svg) reflects the curve in the ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg)-axis. The graph of ![](images/10/103e3884f47f4bb0de41a1498e867b0523672c04de75345dbac027589882ae98.svg) is shown below.\n\n![](images/ee/eef724b522e133a2a537d1b6e1406bdbf17fe285ea43c278888ab4a4bc9fa58c.png)\n\nMultiplying the variable ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg) by ![](images/66/66ef4b5796888b4025ee2d8b3d516ec80741b341db9389696b6e77a4af5208d8.svg) reflects the curve in the ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-axis. The graph of ![](images/22/22049b72df0ed12fbbdc61eba867bc52a0786ea81fb6b26f35a2f82bcd1bc5b1.svg) is shown below.\n\n![](images/78/782eade24c5ab9e1af679f0a310fac2d3e20805d40ee97c695ea214ac71cf2f0.png)\n\nNote that ![](images/22/22049b72df0ed12fbbdc61eba867bc52a0786ea81fb6b26f35a2f82bcd1bc5b1.svg) is only defined for negative numbers and zero.\n\nNow, suppose we want to sketch the graph of ![](images/da/dac5078fc454b1978d14cbf61abe357b898c81885b4ed0274d469de53efaa1f3.svg)\n\nTo obtain the graph of ![](images/ef/ef1b3a5890e7db48752670eeaa86a7499678b614b78b767d4d3a8ed22fc55792.svg) we can perform the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of ![](images/98/981b16229c80f6cdc59aa58acdf4e0c05ecdb93cf05b5f4da61b2f7db0b03802.svg)\n\n- Reflect the graph in the ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg)-axis to get the graph of ![](images/7c/7c760b28b0fcf32a1f8a2b63c8383d8bc0b667ef484b994478f0c157c36519f0.svg)\n\n![](images/b9/b95995b8ee5595d774f02d2c03c1170cc443b8f06f6ccbc634eeeb2aebe86357.png)\n\n- Translate the result to the right by ![](images/f5/f5f3224583db57b9cfe323c8489ef5e5271000002b5ea253eb98fd067a858b2d.svg) units to get the graph of ![](images/74/7458914f9f50a584f281fd213e9bd3ce60d33422fbbd6e679e411c342fd87d1a.svg)\n\n- Translate the result up by ![](images/6c/6cb44f25e489afb06ec62d2e95c4d235ece77eb36e2327b856264d2fb8b22c21.svg) units to get the graph of ![](images/da/dac5078fc454b1978d14cbf61abe357b898c81885b4ed0274d469de53efaa1f3.svg)\n\n![](images/26/263ea3a28314da17ba084bcb512976deb73483dfaa3ad149845c35634ae1d4a4.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "55172b36-dabd-52b3-8195-cbe97b913cc0" :tutorial/math-academy-id 4777 :tutorial/title "Reflections"} :step/id #uuid "aa82b019-f24d-5baa-8ff4-93fdb90e7024" :step/math-academy-id 464542 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111665}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111665 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110710 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110533 :question/id #uuid "4ffc1494-2efd-581c-a58e-d1e9a8a2dfc4" :question/math-academy-id "e-7939"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "adbab69f-d3db-5162-9c21-0402b95e0c74" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048753}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111160} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111163} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557272}] :knowledge-point/title "Graphing a Reflected Square Root Function Containing One Translation"} :step/id #uuid "7124301f-084e-5b5d-b8c2-4b15e1bdd17e" :step/math-academy-id 464543 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111666}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111666 :step/content {:db/id 